cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "micro-lab: a verified market-microstructure research platform"
abstract: >-
  Reconstructs NASDAQ limit order books from LOBSTER sample data (verified
  against LOBSTER's reference book by an exact per-event transition invariant)
  and replicates canonical order-flow results — order-flow imbalance, queue
  imbalance, trade-sign long memory, and price impact — with HAC-robust
  confidence intervals, purged walk-forward cross-validation, and
  false-discovery-rate control. The statistics pipeline is itself verified
  against a ground-truth-injectable order-flow simulator before touching real
  data. Descriptive research only; no PnL or tradability claims.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mar
    given-names: William
repository-code: "https://github.com/billdmar/micro-lab"
url: "https://github.com/billdmar/micro-lab"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
keywords:
  - market-microstructure
  - limit-order-book
  - order-flow-imbalance
  - quantitative-finance
  - reproducible-research
references:
  - type: data
    title: "LOBSTER: Limit Order Book System — the Efficient Reconstructor (NASDAQ sample data)"
    url: "https://lobsterdata.com"
    notes: >-
      Sample data used under LOBSTER's academic-use terms; not redistributed in
      this repository (downloaded at build time by scripts/get_data.sh).
